[Music]  hey everyone it's Jonah here so I've put  together a four week belly fat challenge  for you nope we are not doing 100  crunches okay we know that we cannot  spot reduce fat  hence doing 100 of 1000 crunches every  single they were not work this workout  will be combining core exercises to  really strengthen your core and also  cardio exercises to elevate your heart  rate and also to burn that belly fat a  layer off for the first and second week  the goal is to complete two sets for the  third and fourth week we want to  challenge yourself even more and  complete three sets  so this workout will be based on  repetitions and also time I'm good to  take you through each week let's do it  so let's start with the exercises for  week 1 and also week 3 the aim is to  complete 25 repetitions for each  exercise first full extension fully  extend both arms and legs straight out  crunch in and bring your knees to with  the chest and arms touching the ankles  by lifting your shoulders slightly off  the floor you will feel the upper and  lower abs engaged only lower your legs  as far as you can without arching your  lower back beginners you can bend your  knees slightly  this next exercise is my favorite half  of the attacks support your upper body  and keep your shoulders relaxed keep  both legs together engage your lower abs  and lift them straight up towards the  ceiling then slowly lower down your legs  close to the floor and lift them back up  the guiness again you can choose to keep  your knees slightly bent now let's move  on and focus on your cardio let's do  jump squats stand shoulder width apart  push your butt back and lower yourself  into a deep squat using the force from  your legs lift your body off the floor  into a jump land gently keeping your  knees bent remember to push from your  heels not from your toes okay  this exercise will elevate your heart  rate and burn that stubborn belly fat  let's get back down onto the floor and  do the fourth core exercise four times  apps we want to alternate by lifting and  lowering one leg at a time don't rest  your heels on the floor throughout the  workout so you have to really keep your  core engaged  this continuous motion will create  tension on your lower abs and trust me  you will feel the burn this next workout  focuses on your obliques windshield  wiper to keep your upper body in  position spread both arms out to your  sides now bring both legs straight up  and lower them down to the left side in  a slow and controlled manner using your  core strength bring both legs back to  the center and then lower to the  opposite side to fully engage your  obliques keep your upper body in  position at all times and we want to end  a circuit with another cardio bursting  workout your favourite burpees if you're  a beginner you can choose not to jump  and simply step up aim to complete 25  repetitions in the shortest time  possible  don't stop okay keep your heart rate  elevated and only take one minute break  once you have completed the entire  circuit now let's move on to week two  and for the exercises will be time-based  we want to do each workout for 30  seconds with 10 seconds rest in between  there will be lots of plank exercises  for this week so the first exercise is  plank hip dip get into a solid plank  position keeping your back flat and body  in a straight line  dip your hip to the left and to the  right in a controlled manner avoid  arching your lower back or piking your  butt up so you really have to tighten  your core keep going for 30 seconds stay  strong alright this is your first  workout next spider-man plank get into a  high plank position pumps directly under  your shoulders in a straight line  keeping your elbows slightly bent  bring your right knee towards your right  elbow return to plank position  and alternate on the other side if you  want  killer abs do this let's move on to a  cardio based core exercise plank jacks  so maintain at the high plank position  jump both legs out to a wide stance and  jump both legs back in again when you're  performing plank exercises always  remember to keep your back flat so no  arching or piking your butt up in the  air suck your belly in this will really  give you a strong core working on a core  strength it does not always mean big  movements just by holding a certain  position it can strengthen those deep  core muscles  so the fourth core workout is half the  boot keep your chest up back flat and  lean back slightly lift both legs off  the floor and keep your knees slightly  bent toes pointed maintain this position  for 30 seconds and I want you to clap  your hands up and under your legs next  lie flat on your back keeping your hands  by your head lift your shoulders and  both legs few inches off the floor the  move your legs up and down in a  fluttering motion keep the movement  small this will make your lower abs work  a lot harder beginners you can choose to  rest your shoulders and head on the mat  and the final workout will be another  cardio based exercise Kronus I love and  hate this workout it is so effective but  extremely tiring at the same time start  in a high plank position and bring your  right leg close to your right pump as  you jump your right leg back  simultaneously jump your left leg  forward bringing it close to your left  pump don't stop this will elevate your  heart rate and you will be burning lots  of calories and of course burning the  stubborn belly fat beginners you can  remove the jumping motion and just step  forward and back alternating between the  legs always keep you  chest open and look forward so these are  all the exercises for week two and four  again the aim is to complete at least  two circuits in week two and increase  that to three to four circuits in week  four of course you can take a one-minute  rest in between circuits if you're a  beginner then take a longer rest and to  do this challenge every day all right  you can end your workout with this  challenge if you keep this routine  consistent you will get stronger and you  will see the difference in four weeks be  sure to like this video share and  challenge your friends subscribe to my  youtube channel for more workout videos  and workout challenges do also turn on  your notification button so that you  won't get notified every time I share a  new video all the best

